spi-imx: a controller without DMA channels is not an error

A controller whose device-tree node carries no dmas runs PIO, which is
how the Glowforge sensor PIC's ecspi2 is described on purpose (3-byte
transactions; the pulse ring stays the SDMA's only client).
dma_request_chan() answers -ENODEV for the missing description and the
probe logged it at ERR level at every boot before falling back to PIO.
Keep the message for real failures; stay quiet when no channel is
described.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-imx.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-imx.c
@@ -1382,7 +1382,8 @@ static int spi_imx_sdma_init(struct device *dev, struct spi_imx_data *spi_imx,
 	controller->dma_tx = dma_request_chan(dev, "tx");
 	if (IS_ERR(controller->dma_tx)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(controller->dma_tx);
-		dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "can't get the TX DMA channel!\n");
+		if (ret != -ENODEV)
+			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "can't get the TX DMA channel!\n");
 		controller->dma_tx = NULL;
 		goto err;
 	}
@@ -1391,7 +1392,8 @@ static int spi_imx_sdma_init(struct device *dev, struct spi_imx_data *spi_imx,
 	controller->dma_rx = dma_request_chan(dev, "rx");
 	if (IS_ERR(controller->dma_rx)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(controller->dma_rx);
-		dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "can't get the RX DMA channel!\n");
+		if (ret != -ENODEV)
+			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "can't get the RX DMA channel!\n");
 		controller->dma_rx = NULL;
 		goto err;
 	}
